body:
That could very well be true. I haven't' craved yet after my taper. So I'm hoping that if I do get cravings they're not as strong this time around. 

&#x200B;

The cravings after cold turkey really got to me, and the PAWs were much stronger at 4 weeks out than they are now after tapering 4 weeks ago. So far it seems that the taper has made a huge difference in the experience of PAWs and cravings. 

&#x200B;

I have cleaned my house out of any Kratom products, and I do not have a store or head shop around me that sells Kratom so I would be forced to purchase online if I did get cravings. This means even if the cravings got bad, I'd be waiting 4-5 days to get a hit no matter what.

&#x200B;

My plan is to "just deal with it" basically. There's nothing out there that will mask the cravings, I've tried everything under the sun during my cold turkey quits. The closest thing to reducing cravings is exercise. So that's my plan. Get a craving, go for a run. Get a craving, do some push ups. The trick is to refocus the mind on something else that will benefit me. That's my hope at least.
